jobs.description:
Ideal Candidate
•    Master degree in either Mechanical, Electrical or Software Engineering or other relevant studies;
•    Proven experience in the railway industry/ experience in the signalling railway activities is an asset.
•    Proven experience within railway industry using conventional and/or CBTC signalling technologies is a major asset;
•    Strong experience and broad set of engineering skills across the full system lifecycle (requirements, design, quality/test, commissioning, etc.);
•    General knowledge of industry standards and regulations;
•    Excellent verbal and written communication skills in English. French or Swedish or Danish is an asset.
•    Ability to work in an international and dynamic environment;
•    Autonomous, sense of initiative and detail oriented;
•    Strong analytical and problem solving skills;
 To strengthen our Scandinavian Railway Signalling team, we are looking for motivated and dynamic consultants with expertise in Railway Signalling solutions. They will play a challenging role and be key players in the success of our clients’ projects.

We are looking for motivated and dynamic Railway Signalling Engineers to strengthen our Scandinavian Team.
As a Railway Signalling Engineer you will support our clients by:
•    Offer expert consultancy services with strong added value in the development, design and delivery of signal testing solutions to existing and new clients related to the transportation industry;
•    Participate in project development by giving valued insights on client specifications and deliverables;
•    Analyze customer technical specifications in terms of railway principles and technology requirements;
•    Interact with internal and external multidisciplinary teams to coordinate and achieve project objectives in a timely manner;
•    Act as a mentor to team-members;
•    Ensure technical communication with stakeholders across different level of management;
•    Measure and improve project quality and performance (KPI);
•    Follow-up project progress.

Other responsibilities may include:
Work closely with Management and Business development team to grow the practice in your geographical area, this will include:
•    Work on material to support presentation to clients
•    Pitch & Present to client the services Amaris is offering
•    Work on commercial and technical proposal with the business development team
•    Assess and evaluate new potential recruits in Amaris team
 Amaris is an independent, international Technologies and Management Consulting Group. Created in 2007, Amaris is already established in over 50 countries and supports more than 750 clients worldwide throughout their project's lifecycle. Our expertise covers five areas of innovation: Business and Management, Information Technologies, Engineering and High Technologies, Telecommunications and Biotech and Pharma. With more than 65 offices across the world, the Group offers proximity support to its clients in all their locations and many opportunities of international careers for employees. 

In 2018, Amaris aims to reach a turnover of 260 million euros, 5000 employees and to develop its workforces with the anticipation of a further 2000 new job openings. We expect to triple our workforce within the next few years and reach a leading international position in independent consulting.

Objectives
- Support the Installation Design Manager;
- Perform survey on site (inside the train) and define the technical solution for the Electrical part;
- Report any failure of the Electrical solution during the train fitment in order to address the change in short term period;
Candidate Requirements
Educational Requirements
Master degree in Engineering school / university, specialisation or oriented in 
Electrical design
Desired Knowledge / Experience
- Knowledge of railways is an asset.
- Knowledge of Zuken e3 is an asset.
- - writing skills : clarity, rigor, and concision
- English, minimum FCE
- Danish language is an asset
Behavioural Skills / Competencies
- Team spirit and listening skills;
- Rigor and open-minded;
- Autonomy and perseverance;
- Goodwill and proactivity
